{
  "_about": [
    "Configuration for load_test.py.",
    "packs: pack folders to build and load together (globs; the highest match is used).",
    "layout: dual builds both the singular (1.21+) and plural (1.14 to 1.20) data folders, as the released zips do; singular is what a plain MPP export produces.",
    "versions: every Minecraft version to test, with the VERSION$minecraft.current value DatapackManager must detect there (golden values, recorded from real servers).",
    "quick: the subset --quick runs.",
    "resources: version windows for resources that are meant to load only on some versions. The first matching rule wins; anything without a rule must load on every tested version.",
    "  loads: A..B, A.., ..B, never; {name} is the version in the resource's own name.",
    "  must_fail_outside: the resource must also fail to load outside its window (version probes)."
  ],
